<h1>COURSE OVERVIEW &amp; FACILITATOR PREPARATION</h1>

<h2>Programme Purpose</h2>
<p>Presentation Skills V3 is a targeted, full-day instructor-led training session that equips team members across Tesla UK with the practical skills needed to communicate, present, and facilitate to a professional standard. The ability to communicate with confidence is not limited to formal training delivery. Many individuals across Tesla UK interact daily in contexts that demand clarity, composure, and presence &mdash; internal meetings, cross-functional calls, leadership presentations, job interviews, and customer and contractor interactions &mdash; yet rarely receive structured development in how to do this effectively.</p>

<h2>Programme Objective</h2>
<p>To deliver V3 of the Presentation Skills ILT that directly addresses the gap in structured communication development through four integrated pillars:</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Public Speaking &amp; Personal Presence:</strong> Developing composure, clarity, and confidence when speaking in group settings &mdash; including internal meetings, Microsoft Teams calls, panel interviews, and cross-functional forums &mdash; where individuals need to represent themselves and their ideas credibly</li>
    <li><strong>Business Cases, Pitches &amp; Structured Discussions:</strong> Equipping participants with frameworks for presenting ideas, proposals, and recommendations in a way that is logical, persuasive, and appropriate for the audience &mdash; whether pitching to a senior leadership team, presenting a business case for investment, or making a case for operational change</li>
    <li><strong>PowerPoint &amp; Visual Content Design:</strong> Building the ability to create structured, visually effective materials that support and strengthen a message rather than undermine it</li>
    <li><strong>Facilitation Skills:</strong> Developing the ability to read a room, manage group dynamics, draw out contribution from quieter individuals, handle challenging questions or pushback, and keep energy and focus consistent across a session &mdash; including how to open with impact, use questioning techniques, manage time without losing depth, and close in a way that drives retention and action</li>
</ol>

<h2>Target Outcome</h2>
<p>Confident and capable team members across Tesla UK who can present, facilitate, and communicate with credibility across all professional contexts:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Individuals who previously struggled with visibility in meetings, on calls, or in high-stakes conversations develop the composure and structure to communicate their ideas clearly and credibly, regardless of the audience or setting</li>
    <li>Participants are able to deliver structured, engaging, and professional presentations to varied audiences, moving beyond information transfer to communication that genuinely lands and drives action</li>
    <li>Participants move beyond passive information delivery to actively managing groups, handling dynamics, drawing out contribution, responding to challenge, and maintaining energy and focus</li>
    <li>Greater personal confidence in high-stakes moments &mdash; whether in a panel interview, a leadership presentation, a Teams call, or a cross-functional forum &mdash; participants have practical tools and rehearsed experience to perform under pressure</li>
</ul>

<h2>Six Core Teaching Themes</h2>
<p>The following six themes are woven throughout every module and activity. They are not standalone topics but lenses that the facilitator must constantly reinforce:</p>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:30%;">Theme</th><th>Definition</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Audience Empathy</strong></td><td>Shifting the focus from &ldquo;what I want to say&rdquo; to &ldquo;what they need to hear.&rdquo; Understanding the differing priorities of stakeholders, team members, and senior leadership.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Strategic Storytelling</strong></td><td>Translating complex data or abstract concepts into a compelling narrative. The ability to show a clear path forward that people can buy into.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Making the Complex Simple</strong></td><td>Filtering out excessive background noise or jargon to deliver headlines first, saving granular details for the appendix or Q&amp;A.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Executive Presence</strong></td><td>Projecting calm confidence, commanding attention naturally, and effectively using strategic pauses and vocal modulation.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Active Listening</strong></td><td>Paying close attention to the audience&rsquo;s reactions, body language, and feedback during the session to dynamically adapt delivery.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Managing Q&amp;A and Conflict</strong></td><td>Anticipating objections, fielding questions with composure, and steering feedback toward actionable results.</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Facilitator Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Review all materials, handouts, slide decks, and video clips at least 48 hours before delivery</li>
    <li>Prepare the room layout in a U-shape or cabaret style &mdash; participants must be able to see each other and a clear presentation area</li>
    <li>Test all AV equipment including projector/screen, clicker, speakers, webcam, and any recording devices</li>
    <li>Confirm a working Microsoft Teams setup with a second device (laptop or tablet) for the Virtual Presence drill in Module 3</li>
    <li>Source and test all video exemplar clips (see Appendix E for sourcing guide and cue sheet)</li>
    <li>Print all participant handouts (see Appendix B) &mdash; one pack per participant plus two spares</li>
    <li>Prepare a flip chart with the &ldquo;Parking Lot&rdquo; header for capturing off-topic questions</li>
    <li>Have a timer visible (phone on a stand or wall clock) &mdash; timed activities run throughout the day</li>
    <li>Prepare name tent cards or table name cards for each participant</li>
    <li>Review the Inclusivity &amp; Accessibility section below and adapt activities if needed based on known participant needs</li>
    <li>Send the pre-session communication to participants (see Post-Session Transfer section) at least 5 working days before the session</li>
</ul>

