<h1>APPENDIX B: PARTICIPANT HANDOUTS &amp; TEMPLATES</h1>

<h2>Handout 1: Audience Empathy Worksheet</h2>
<p><em>One per participant.</em></p>
<table>
<tr><th colspan="2" style="background-color:#333333;">AUDIENCE EMPATHY WORKSHEET</th></tr>
<tr><td style="width:40%; background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>My presentation / meeting / communication:</strong></td><td>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Q1: Who is in the room?</strong><br><em>(Names, roles, priorities, knowledge level)</em></td><td>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Q2: What do they already know?</strong><br><em>(Existing knowledge, context, previous exposure)</em></td><td>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Q3: What do they need to decide or do after this?</strong><br><em>(The action or decision you are driving toward)</em></td><td>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Q4: What is the one thing they must remember?</strong><br><em>(If they forget 90%, what is the 10% that sticks?)</em></td><td>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Handout 2: One-Slide Challenge Worksheet</h2>
<p><em>One per participant.</em></p>
<table>
<tr><th colspan="2" style="background-color:#333333;">ONE-SLIDE CHALLENGE</th></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Your project / initiative / piece of work:</strong> &nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2" style="text-align:center; padding:16pt; border:2px solid #c00000;">
<p style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; color:#c00000;">HEADLINE (max 10 words):</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom:8pt;">&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p>
<p style="font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt;">Supporting Point 1 (max 15 words):</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom:8pt;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="font-weight:bold;">Supporting Point 2 (max 15 words):</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom:8pt;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="font-weight:bold;">Supporting Point 3 (max 15 words):</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom:8pt;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; color:#c00000;">THE ASK / NEXT STEP (one sentence):</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid #ccc; padding-bottom:8pt;">&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</p>
</td></tr>
<tr><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Partner feedback:</strong> Could they understand it without extra explanation? What would they cut or clarify?<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Handout 3: Business Case Template</h2>
<p><em>One per participant.</em></p>
<table>
<tr><th colspan="2" style="background-color:#333333;">BUSINESS CASE TEMPLATE</th></tr>
<tr><td style="width:30%; background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>PREP Quick Version</strong></td><td>
<strong>P &mdash; Point:</strong> State your recommendation.<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>R &mdash; Reason:</strong> Why?<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>E &mdash; Example:</strong> Make it real.<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>P &mdash; Point (restated):</strong> Close the loop.<br>&nbsp;
</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f5;"><strong>Five-Box Full Version</strong></td><td>
<strong>1. Context &amp; Problem Statement:</strong><br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>2. Proposed Solution:</strong><br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>3. Cost &amp; Resources Required:</strong><br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>4. Expected Outcome &amp; Benefit:</strong><br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;<br>
<strong>5. Risk &amp; Mitigation:</strong><br>&nbsp;<br>&nbsp;
</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Handout 4: Key Frameworks Reference Card</h2>
<p><em>Single-page reference card for participants to keep.</em></p>
<table>
<tr><th style="background-color:#333333;" colspan="2">PRESENTATION SKILLS V3 &mdash; KEY FRAMEWORKS REFERENCE CARD</th></tr>
<tr><td style="width:30%; background-color:#ffe0e0;"><strong>Audience Empathy<br>4 Questions</strong></td><td>1. Who is in the room? 2. What do they already know? 3. What do they need to decide/do? 4. What is the one thing they must remember?</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#fff3e0;"><strong>SCR+BN Framework</strong></td><td><strong>S</strong>ituation &rarr; <strong>C</strong>omplication &rarr; <strong>R</strong>esolution &rarr; <strong>B</strong>enefit &rarr; <strong>N</strong>ext Step</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#e8f5e9;"><strong>Pyramid Principle</strong></td><td>Start with the answer. Then supporting arguments. Then data (only if asked). Top-down, not bottom-up.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#e3f2fd;"><strong>PREP Framework</strong></td><td><strong>P</strong>oint &rarr; <strong>R</strong>eason &rarr; <strong>E</strong>xample &rarr; <strong>P</strong>oint (restated)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#f3e5f5;"><strong>Executive Presence<br>4 Pillars</strong></td><td>1. Vocal Variety (pace, volume, pitch) 2. Strategic Pause 3. Physicality &amp; Body Language 4. Managing Nerves (box breathing, pre-performance reset, reframe)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#e3f2fd;"><strong>Virtual Presence<br>5 Rules</strong></td><td>1. Camera = eye contact 2. Energy up 20% 3. Frame yourself properly 4. Use chat/reactions strategically 5. Manage screen-share transitions</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#fce4ec;"><strong>Facilitation Open</strong></td><td>Hook &rarr; Purpose &rarr; Contract</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#e0f2f1;"><strong>Facilitation Close</strong></td><td>Summarise &rarr; Assign &rarr; Inspire</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#fff3e0;"><strong>Time Management</strong></td><td>1. Time Contract (tell them how long) 2. Value Check (transparent trade-offs) 3. Parking Lot with Purpose (specific follow-up)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#fff8e1;"><strong>Billboard Test</strong></td><td>If someone driving past at 70mph can&rsquo;t get the message in 3 seconds, the slide is too complex.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#efebe9;"><strong>Q&amp;A Rules</strong></td><td>1. Welcome it 2. Listen fully 3. Acknowledge before answering 4. Bridge if needed 5. &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know&rdquo; with confidence 6. Redirect the persistent challenger</td></tr>
</table>

